.TH KALIP 1 "2026-09-11" "kalip 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kalip \- write disk images to USB, SD and NVMe media
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kalip
.RI [ IMAGE ]
.br
.B kalip
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kalip
writes Linux ISO images and Raspberry Pi OS images to storage media. If
.I IMAGE
is given it is opened on startup; otherwise a file can be chosen from the
interface or fetched from a URL.
.PP
Images may be raw
.RB ( .iso ", " .img ", " .raw )
or compressed with xz, gzip, zstd or zip. The format is detected from the
file's magic bytes, not its extension.
.PP
A URL is queried before anything is transferred: the redirect chain is
followed and the resulting file name, size and content type are reported.
Downloads are cached under
.I ~/.cache/kalip
so writing the same image again does not fetch it twice.
.SH RASPBERRY PI OS
When the image's partition table matches a Raspberry Pi OS layout \(en a FAT
boot partition followed by a Linux root partition \(en first boot settings can
be written to
.I custom.toml
on the boot partition: hostname, user account and password, SSH public keys and
whether password login is permitted, wireless network, keyboard layout and time
zone. This applies to Raspberry Pi OS bookworm and later. Static addressing and
multiple wireless networks are not expressible in that format.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The interface never runs as root. Writing is performed by
.I /usr/libexec/kalip/kalip-helper
which is elevated through polkit under the action
.BR me.soylu.kalip.write .
Because the helper has no graphical interface of its own, this works in Wayland
sessions, where applications that elevate their entire interface cannot connect
to the display.
.PP
The helper re-validates its target independently of the interface. It refuses to
write to any whole device holding a mounted system filesystem
.RI ( / ", " /boot ", " /home ", " /usr ", " /var )
or swap, opens the device with
.B O_EXCL
so the kernel rejects a device still in use, and checks the image against the
device's capacity before writing a byte.
.SH VERIFICATION
With verification enabled the written range is read back and compared by
SHA\-256.
.BR posix_fadvise (2)
is called with
.B POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED
first, so the comparison reads the device rather than the page cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/kalip
Downloaded images.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/kalip/kalip-helper
Privileged helper. Can be run directly under
.BR sudo (8)
for debugging; see
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/me.soylu.kalip.policy
polkit action definition.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The image could not be written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsblk (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR dd (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Orkun Soylu <103385766+orkun-soylu@users.noreply.github.com>
